    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SAFETY CARD\nB737-200RS\nFrontier\nI RLINE S\nThe Spirit of the West\nPlease obey the \"No Smoking\" and \"Fasten Seatbelt\" signs\nand all instructions given by your crew members.\nFOR THE SAFETY OF OTHERS PLEASE DO NOT REMOVE\nTHIS CARD FROM THE AIRCRAFT",
      ":01\n2\n3\n:03\n4\n:05\n:07\n:10\nFlotation Cushions\n••••••••••••..П...\nTS 0110\nCopyright\nCode 94100\n1994 SAFEAIR, INC.Olympia, WA., (206)754-5837. All Rights Reserved.\n2002.127.312",
      "Exit Seating Criteria\nIf you are seated in an emergency\nexit seat, please review the following.\nFederal Aviation Regulations require\nthat passengers seated in these seats\nmeet the selection criteria and are\nwilling and able to operate the exit\nand assist others in the event of an\nemergency in which a crewmember\nis not available to do so.\nPlease identify the exit nearest to you\nand review the corresponding\nfunctions found on this Safety Card.\nPlease contact your Flight Attendant\nfor reseating if you have a condition,\nwhich is not apparent, that would\nprevent you from performing the\nfunctions shown on this Safety Card;\nwould be harmed from doing so; do\nnot wish to do so; or if any of the\nfollowing apply:\n• Mobility, strength or dexterity in\nboth arm and legs is not sufficient\nto perform the functions and assist\nothers, including:\n-Reaching the exit quickly\n- Reaching in every direction for\nmechanisms used\n- Operating the exit\n- Securing the exit open\n-Removing obstructions (maintaining\nbalance while doing so\n-Quickly pass through the exit\n• You are less than 15 years old,\nrequire assistance from someone\nelse to perform one or more of these\nfunctions, or would be prevented\nfrom doing so because of a\ncondition or responsibility, such as\ncaring for a small child.\n• You cannot sufficiently impart\ninformation orally to others or\nunderstand oral crew commands.\n• You cannot read or understand the\nwritten or graphic instructions\nprovided or require assistance\n(other than a hearing aid to hear\nor understand the instructions\nshouted by a crewmember.\n• You do not have the visual capacity\nto assess conditions outside of the\nexit or perform any function described\nwithout the assistance of visual aids\nother than contact lenses or eyeglasses.\nIn the event of an emergency, follow the\ndirections and hand signals of your crew.\nIf a crewmember is not available to assist\nyou, follow the instructions on the\nSafety Card and posted signs. Wait\nuntil the airplane has stopped before\nopening the exit and look through the\nwindow, assessing conditions (looking\nfor smoke, fire or obstructions) to\ndetermine whether it is safe to proceed.\nIf it is safe to do so, operate the exit and\nassist others according to the instructions.\nAssess, select and follow a safe path\naway from the airplane.\nYour Flight Attendants will be glad to\nanswer any questions you might have.\nRESTRICTED AT ALL TIMES\nCelluar\nPhones\nButane\nLighters\nD Tampering\nwith lavatory smoke\nSmoking\nOnboard Aircraft\nRESTRICTED AT TIMES\nYour flight crew will advise when permitted\nComputers\nRadios\nR/C Toys\nVideo Games\nEXIT",
      "B\nB\nB\n000000\n100000\nC) 1994 SAFEAIR, INC.\n94100"
    ],
